<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q96F10">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_818408f621a53437c7874d7f80b04fe2" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Diamine acetyltransferase 2</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q96F10" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_SAT2_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SAT2_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Polyamine N-acetyltransferase 2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SSAT2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.3.1.57</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Thialysine N-epsilon-acetyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SAT2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Spermidine/spermine N(1)-acetyltransferase 2</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_15296_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Enzyme which catalyzes the acetylation of polyamines.Substrate specificity: norspermidine &gt; spermidine = spermine &gt;&gt;N(1)acetylspermine = putrescine.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=acetyl-CoA + an alkane-alpha,omega-diamine = an N-acetylalkane-alpha,omega-diamine + CoA + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11116, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9766, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9767,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:57287, ChEBI:CHEBI:57288,ChEBI:CHEBI:70977, ChEBI:CHEBI:70988; EC=2.3.1.57;PATHWAY: Amine and polyamine degradation; putrescine degradation;N-acetylputrescine from putrescine: step 1/1.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16596569}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm. Note=Intracellular organelles.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed.INDUCTION: Not inducible by polyamine analogs.MISCELLANEOUS: Under physiological conditions, SSAT2 is expressedat lower level that SSAT1 (SSAT). Many tissues express only SSAT1,several tissues express both SSAT1 and SSAT2, and bone, cervix,ovary and pineal gland expressed only SSAT2.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acetyltransferase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SAT2_HUMAN Reviewed; 170 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q96F10_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_597998</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_2BEI_see-also</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_112483</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_112483</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference81736</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

