<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P14920">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_35af76a326668bd749d50a78504d5175" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_92d7f2a2d661b5d89b973f6cbb3b87c1" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">D-amino-acid oxidase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_DAO_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P14920" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OXDA_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DAO</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.4.3.3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DAAO</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DAMOX</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_1610</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_15917_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Regulates the level of the neuromodulator D-serine inthe brain. Has high activity towards D-DOPA and contributes todopamine synthesis. Could act as a detoxifying agent which removesD-amino acids accumulated during aging. Acts on a variety of D-amino acids with a preference for those having small hydrophobicside chains followed by those bearing polar, aromatic, and basicgroups. Does not act on acidic amino acids.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a D-alpha-amino acid + H2O + O2 = a 2-oxocarboxylate +H2O2 + NH4(+); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21816, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:15379, ChEBI:CHEBI:16240, ChEBI:CHEBI:28938,ChEBI:CHEBI:35179, ChEBI:CHEBI:59871; EC=1.4.3.3;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322};COFACTOR:Name=FAD; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57692;BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=3.6 mM for D-serine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};KM=1.7 mM for D-proline {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};KM=1.1 mM for D-tyrosine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};KM=1.5 mM for D-DOPA {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};KM=1.2 mM for D-phenylalanine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};KM=0.9 mM for D-alanine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17303072};SUBUNIT: Homodimer (PubMed:17088322, PubMed:18455394). Interactswith DAOA (PubMed:12364586). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12364586,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17088322, ECO:0000269|PubMed:18455394}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Peroxisome.DISEASE: Schizophrenia (SCZD) [MIM:181500]: A complex,multifactorial psychotic disorder or group of disorderscharacterized by disturbances in the form and content of thought(e.g. delusions, hallucinations), in mood (e.g. inappropriateaffect), in sense of self and relationship to the external world(e.g. loss of ego boundaries, withdrawal), and in behavior (e.gbizarre or apparently purposeless behavior). Although it affectsemotions, it is distinguished from mood disorders in which suchdisturbances are primary. Similarly, there may be mild impairmentof cognitive function, and it is distinguished from the dementiasin which disturbed cognitive function is considered primary. Somepatients manifest schizophrenic as well as bipolar disordersymptoms and are often given the diagnosis of schizoaffectivedisorder. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12364586}. Note=Diseasesusceptibility may be associated with variations affecting thegene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the DAMOX/DASOX family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
