<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q53H96">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_1eda80c3787e7ca7aabe9519b5cc29bc" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_fc29bf2ed93bcaa07ef72df2930c5d32" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_04727a64df5ecf9a299f94154cbff1bb" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Pyrroline-5-carboxylate reductase 3</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q53H96" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_PYCR3_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">P5CR3_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PYCRL</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">P5C reductase 3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">P5CR 3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PYCR3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Pyrroline-5-carboxylate reductase-like protein</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.5.1.2</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_65263</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/A0A0A0MQS1</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_15196_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_B5MD87_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">P5CR3_HUMAN Reviewed; 274 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Enzyme that catalyzes the last step in prolinebiosynthesis. Proline is synthesized from either glutamate orornithine; both are converted to pyrroline-5-carboxylate (P5C),and then to proline via pyrroline-5-carboxylate reductases(PYCRs). PYCRL is exclusively linked to the conversion ofornithine to proline. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=L-proline + NADP(+) = 1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate + 2 H(+)+ NADPH; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:14109, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:15893, ChEBI:CHEBI:57783, ChEBI:CHEBI:58349,ChEBI:CHEBI:60039; EC=1.5.1.2;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=L-proline + NAD(+) = 1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate + 2 H(+) +NADH; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:14105, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:15893, ChEBI:CHEBI:57540, ChEBI:CHEBI:57945,ChEBI:CHEBI:60039; EC=1.5.1.2;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Not inhibited by proline.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.42 mM for NADH {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};KM=0.37 mM for NADPH {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};KM=4.64 mM for pyrroline-5-carboxylate (in the presence of NADH){ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};KM=0.38 mM for pyrroline-5-carboxylate (in the presence ofNADPH) {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};Note=kcat is 197 sec(-1) for the NADH-dependent reduction ofpyrroline-5-carboxylate. kcat is 35 sec(-1) for the NADPH-dependent reduction of pyrroline-5-carboxylate.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808};PATHWAY: Amino-acid biosynthesis; L-proline biosynthesis; L-proline from L-glutamate 5-semialdehyde: step 1/1.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808}.SUBUNIT: Homodecamer; composed of 5 homodimers.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P32322}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23024808}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q53H96-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q53H96-2; Sequence=VSP_057219;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the pyrroline-5-carboxylate reductasefamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAD96405.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally shortened.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAD96405.1; Type=Miscellaneous discrepancy; Note=Chimeric cDNA.; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q53H96_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_006725155</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_A0A0A0MQS1_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference101461</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

