 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Plays an important role in the de novo pathway and inthe salvage pathway of purine nucleotide biosynthesis. Catalyzesthe first committed step in the biosynthesis of AMP from IMP.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=GTP + IMP + L-aspartate = GDP + 2 H(+) + N(6)-(1,2-dicarboxyethyl)-AMP + phosphate; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:15753,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:29991, ChEBI:CHEBI:37565,ChEBI:CHEBI:43474, ChEBI:CHEBI:57567, ChEBI:CHEBI:58053,ChEBI:CHEBI:58189; EC=6.3.4.4; Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127};COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127};Note=Binds 1 Mg(2+) ion per subunit. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127};PATHWAY: Purine metabolism; AMP biosynthesis via de novo pathway;AMP from IMP: step 1/2. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127}.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm. Note=Partially associated withparticulate fractions.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adenylosuccinate synthetase family.{ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03127}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

