<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P23378">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_0f05d2db086748a9e8a88083b56c1b16" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_b097c1362b1ae0c3bfee293209c4db2d" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_061c4815b88e1e0cec33b0fd5f1a471d" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_c4804634523fd34a53776449f4396cb2" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_714608d9f5607cca2509c88b2c0e3218" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_6bf799d1c325b976b1c4fdfae4b94826" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_9285f3895b7c33fbf113f11e651c6f41" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glycine dehydrogenase (decarboxylating), mitochondrial</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P23378" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_GLDC_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCSP_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glycine cleavage system P protein</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glycine dehydrogenase (aminomethyl-transferring)</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.4.4.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GLDC</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCSP</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glycine decarboxylase</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_2731</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCSP_HUMAN Reviewed; 1020 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: The glycine cleavage system catalyzes the degradation ofglycine. The P protein (GLDC) binds the alpha-amino group ofglycine through its pyridoxal phosphate cofactor; CO(2) isreleased and the remaining methylamine moiety is then transferredto the lipoamide cofactor of the H protein (GCSH).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:1993704, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1996985,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28244183}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=glycine + H(+) + N(6)-lipoyl-L-lysyl-[glycine-cleavagecomplex H protein] = (R)-N(6)-(S(8)-aminomethyldihydrolipoyl)-L-lysyl-[glycine-cleavage complex H protein] + CO2;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:24304, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10494, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:10495, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:16526,ChEBI:CHEBI:57305, ChEBI:CHEBI:83099, ChEBI:CHEBI:83143;EC=1.4.4.2; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:1993704,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1996985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28244183};COFACTOR:Name=pyridoxal 5&apos;-phosphate; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:597326;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15505};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Stimulated by lipoic acid. Inhibited inpresence of methylamine (By similarity).{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15505}.SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity). Interacts with GCSH (Bysimilarity). The glycine cleavage system is composed of fourproteins: P (GLDC), T (GCST), L (DLD) and H (GCSH).{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15505}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28244183}.DISEASE: Non-ketotic hyperglycinemia (NKH) [MIM:605899]: Autosomalrecessive disease characterized by accumulation of a large amountof glycine in body fluid and by severe neurological symptoms.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:11286506, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11592811,ECO:0000269|PubMed:1634607, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1996985,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28244183, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28737873}.Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the generepresented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the GcvP family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_000161</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P23378_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ra.cs.uni-tuebingen.de/software/KEGGtranslator/EC1442.eref</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_01996_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

